# The natural expression grammar — LEFT-recursive (E -> E + T), which is how you
# get left associativity (Module 6) but exactly what recursive descent cannot
# parse (Module 19). Eliminating direct left recursion here yields the
# E -> T E' / E' -> + T E' | epsilon grammar Modules 19-22 have been using.
%start E
E -> E + T | T
T -> T * F | F
F -> ( E ) | id | num
